</div><div data-type="note" id="fs-id1167063877563" class="snap-lab ui-has-child-title"><header><h3 class="os-title" data-type="title">
  <span class="os-title-label">Snap Lab</span>
</h3></header><section>
<div class="os-note-body"><h4 data-type="title" class="os-subtitle">
  <span class="os-subtitle-label">Concave and Convex Mirrors</span>
</h4>

<ul id="fs-id1167067276622" class="materials">
<li>Silver spoon and silver polish, or a new spoon made of any shiny metal</li>
</ul>
<p id="fs-id1164566695373">Instructions</p>
<div data-type="list" id="fs-id1167067272160"><div data-type="title">Procedure</div><ol>
<li>Choose any small object with a top and a bottom, such as a short nail or tack, or a coin, such as a quarter. Observe the object’s reflection on the back of the spoon.</li>
<li>Observe the reflection of the object on the front (bowl side) of the spoon when held away from the spoon at a distance of several inches.</li>
<li>Observe the image while slowly moving the small object toward the bowl of the spoon. Continue until the object is all the way inside the bowl of the spoon.</li>
<li>You should s